# ============================================================
#  CHAIN: Ilse Dumont (expansion)
#  Kael's younger sister, raised by the Hollow cult. She takes a room
#  above the bakery in year 2 (hs_ilse_arrives, X11); you meet her
#  there if you follow the lead, or at the gates (hs_kael_sister).
#    ilse_village -> ilse_frost_lessons -> ilse_grey_returns
#      -> (ilse_saved) ilse_kael_reunion / ilse_northern_letter / ilse_farewell
#      -> (ilse_taken) she is gone north
# ============================================================

@thread ilse
actor: ilse
name: Ilse's winter
premise: Kael's sister, in white furs, in a village that has never seen anyone like her.
journal:
  seen(ilse_village) > 0: In the village bakery a girl in white furs froze her coin to the counter. She has Kael's eyes. Her name is Ilse.
  seen(ilse_frost_lessons) > 0: Ilse traded you Northern frost-craft for news of her brother.
  flag(ilse_taken) and seen(ilse_grey_returns) > 0: When the man in grey came for her in the lane, Ilse went with him.
  flag(ilse_saved): When the man in grey came for her, she stepped out from under his hand. You were there.
  flag(dumont_reunited): Kael and Ilse talked at last: a careful arm's length apart, then less.
  flag(ilse_went_north): Ilse took the dawn barge north, to tell her family it's over.
  flag(ilse_decided) and not flag(ilse_went_north): Ilse stayed, and sewed a sliver of winter into your collar in case they come.
  flag(ilse_goodbye): Under one snowing tree in blossom, Ilse said goodbye.
status:
  resolved: flag(ilse_goodbye) or flag(ilse_went_north) or flag(dumont_reunited)
  missed: flag(ilse_taken) and not flag(ilse_saved)

@event ilse_village
title: The Girl at the Bakery
place: village
class: story
tone: eerie
when: not met(ilse) and (flag(ilse_in_village) or flag(met_sister))
weight: 20
art: snow
tags: mystery hollowstar
thread: ilse
scene: A village bakery counter, a pale girl in white furs pushing a coin that is visibly frosted across the wood, a baffled baker.
text: In the village bakery a girl in white furs is trying to pay for a bun with a coin so cold it has frozen to the counter. The baker is losing patience. You recognise those eyes: they're Kael's. "Ilse," she says, before you ask. "Don't."
> left: Pay for her bun
  meet ilse
  gold -tiny
  rel ilse +medium
  say: She stares at the bun, then at you, as if kindness is a trick she hasn't learned the counter to yet. "Fine," she says. "Thank you. Fine."
> right: Leave her to it
  meet ilse
  rel ilse -tiny
  say: You leave. Through the window you see the coin crack, and the baker's breath freeze in the air. Ilse walks out with the bun. Nobody stops her.

@event ilse_frost_lessons
title: A Trade in Winter
class: story
tone: eerie
trigger: social
when: rel(ilse) >= 3 and not flag(ilse_taken) and not flag(ilse_went_north)
weight: 14
art: snow
tags: magic hollowstar
thread: ilse
scene: A frozen pond at the edge of the woods, a girl in white furs drawing a perfect hexagon of frost in the air, a student copying her clumsily.
text: Ilse finds you by the frozen pond. "My brother won't talk to me. You will. Tell me how he really is, and I'll teach you Northern frost-craft. It's better than anything your professors know."
> left: Tell her the truth about Kael
  rel ilse +large
  arcana +medium
  say: You tell her about the cold hands, {seen(astro_kael_roof): the roof at three in the morning|the nights he doesn't sleep}, the bread. She listens without moving. Then she teaches you to freeze a falling leaf mid-air.
> right: Protect Kael's privacy
  rel ilse -small
  rel kael +small
  arcana +small
  say: "He can tell you himself," you say. Ilse's eyes go flat. But the next day, she's at the pond again. "Fine. I'll teach you anyway. You'll need it." She teaches you badly on purpose for an hour, and then, despite herself, well.

@event ilse_grey_returns
time: night
title: The Man in Grey Comes for Ilse
type: menu
class: story
tone: tense
trigger: social
when: rel(ilse) >= 7 and turn >= 20 and not flag(ilse_saved) and not flag(ilse_taken) and not closed(hollowstar)
weight: 18
art: mask
tags: danger hollowstar
thread: ilse
# Feedback 2026-10-25: his fight was a fixed level 23 (journeyman, no drift); now expert with drift mid, so he keeps up
# with you. v2: three ways to stand between them, one of them a fight; losing any of them, he takes her (and the
# Night gives you one more chance, hs_night_ilse).
scene: A moonlit village lane with every window frosted over, a man in a grey coat with one hand on a girl's shoulder, frost and shadow coiling around them both.
text: A lane behind the bakery, after dark, every window on it frosted over. The man in grey has a hand on Ilse's shoulder and is talking to her softly: "Home. Your mother is waiting. The door is waiting." Ilse's jaw is set and her eyes are wet. She sees you over his shoulder and doesn't call out. She just looks.
> left: Step between them
  hint: Combat. He fights like winter. Lose, and he takes her.
  challenge combat expert drift mid:
    win:
      flag ilse_saved grey_beaten
      rel ilse +large
      renown +small
      alignment +small
      find ilse_truth
      hs_investigation_progress
      say: Your spell breaks his grip. He looks at his frosted glove with mild surprise, bows, and walks into the dark. Ilse is shaking. "Nobody's ever..." she says, and stops, and shouts after him in Northern instead, every word of it a door slammed.
    lose:
      flag ilse_taken
      alignment +small
      find ilse_truth
      hs_investigation_progress
      say: He's breathing hard when it ends, which is somehow worse. When you get up, the lane is empty except for a single white glove in the snow.
> talk: "She's not yours to take."
  hint: Charm. Better if you know what she was raised for.
  challenge negotiate expert +1 if clue(ilse_truth) +1 if rel(ilse) >= 15:
    win:
      flag ilse_saved
      rel ilse +large
      alignment +small
      find ilse_truth
      hs_investigation_progress
      say: You tell him, out loud, in the street, what they raised her for and what she's chosen instead. Ilse says "Yes," very clearly, and steps out from under his hand. He looks at the two of you for a long moment, then bows and walks into the dark.
    lose:
      flag ilse_taken
      mood -medium
      find ilse_truth
      hs_investigation_progress
      say: He agrees with every word, gently, and Ilse's shoulders drop as he talks. When he turns her toward the road, she goes. At the corner she looks back once. In the snow there's a single white glove.
> right: Run for Kael
  hint: Sure, if Kael is here to fetch. She'll know who you went for.
  if met(kael):
    flag ilse_saved
    rel kael +large
    rel ilse -small
    find ilse_truth
    hs_investigation_progress
    say: Kael arrives like a blizzard, shouting her name. The man in grey takes one look at him and leaves without a word. Brother and sister stand in the snow, not touching, not speaking, until Ilse punches him in the arm and the snow stops. "You went for him," she tells you later. "Not for me."
  else:
    flag ilse_taken
    mood -medium
    find ilse_truth
    hs_investigation_progress
    say: By the time you're back with help, the lane is empty. There's frost on the cobbles in the shape of a closed door.

@event ilse_kael_reunion
title: Brother and Sister
class: story
tone: eerie
trigger: social
when: flag(ilse_saved) and met(kael) and not flag(dumont_reunited) and not flag(ilse_went_north)
weight: 16
art: snow
tags: social hollowstar
thread: ilse
scene: Two pale siblings on opposite ends of a frozen jetty, a third person between them holding three cups of tea.
text: Kael and Ilse have been in the same village for weeks and have spoken eleven words to each other. You have three cups of tea, a frozen jetty and a very bad idea.
> left: Sit them both down
  challenge negotiate apprentice+:
    win:
      flag dumont_reunited
      rel kael +large
      rel ilse +large
      say: It takes an hour and two cups of tea are frozen solid. Then Ilse says "I was scared," and Kael says "So was I," and you quietly leave them to it.
    lose:
      rel kael +small
      rel ilse +small
      say: They argue in a language you don't speak, at a temperature you can't endure. But they argue — which, you suspect, is a start.
> right: Let them find their own way
  flag dumont_reunited
  rel kael +small
  rel ilse +small
  say: You leave the tea on the jetty. A week later you see them walking by the lake together, a careful arm's length apart. Then less.

@event ilse_northern_letter
title: A Summons From the North
class: story
tone: eerie
trigger: social
when: flag(ilse_saved) and final_year and not flag(ilse_decided)
weight: 14
art: letter
tags: hollowstar
thread: ilse
scene: A girl holding a letter sealed with a black star, standing at a window that looks north toward far white mountains.
text: A letter with a black-star seal. The Dumont family summons Ilse home. "If I don't go, they'll send someone worse than the man in grey," she says. "If I do go, I could tell them to their faces that it's over. Or they could keep me."
> left: "Go. Tell them it's over."
  flag ilse_decided ilse_went_north
  rel ilse +medium
  say: She leaves on the dawn barge, chin up. Before she goes, she presses her forehead to yours, a Northern farewell. "If I'm not back by graduation," she says, "come and get me."
> right: "Stay. Let them come."
  flag ilse_decided
  rel ilse +large
  gain frost_ward
  say: She stays. She sews a sliver of winter into your collar "in case they do come". Nobody does. Not yet.

@event ilse_farewell
title: Snow in Blossomtide
class: story
tone: light
trigger: social
when: flag(ilse_saved) and final_year and month >= 7 and month <= 9 and not flag(ilse_goodbye) and not flag(ilse_went_north)
weight: 14
art: snow
tags: social
thread: ilse
scene: A single snowflake falling in a spring orchard full of blossom, a girl in white furs catching it on her glove and holding it out.
text: It's spring, the orchard is in full blossom, and it is snowing — gently, over one tree. Ilse is underneath it. "Graduation's soon," she says. "Everyone's leaving. I wanted to give you something before you forgot me."
> left: "I won't forget you."
  flag ilse_goodbye
  rel ilse +large
  gain frost_ward
  mood +medium
  say: She doesn't believe you, but she smiles anyway — the first real smile you've seen on her. She gives you a snowflake that never melts.
> right: Invite her to the graduation
  flag ilse_goodbye
  rel ilse +large
  rel kael +small
  say: "Me? At a graduation?" She looks horrified, and then, slowly, delighted. On the day, she sits next to Kael in the second row and cries more than anyone.
